    "winner": "01__19559867-RESPONSE-BALANCED-10182026.tex",
    "collective_statement_most_likely_to_succeed": "Candidate #2 (01__19559867-RESPONSE-BALANCED-10182026.tex) represents the optimal prosecution response from the perspective of an experienced USPTO pre-examination legal instrument examiner, petitions attorney, and supervisory patent examiner. It flawlessly balances complete statutory compliance with exemplary professional decorum. Procedurally, it correctly invokes 35 U.S.C. \u00a7 21(b) and 37 CFR \u00a7 1.7 to establish that the 2-month deadline falling on Saturday, October 17, 2026, automatically rolled over to Monday, October 19, 2026, making the Sunday, October 18, 2026 filing fully timely within the initial statutory response window while prudently incorporating a protective conditional extension of time under 37 CFR \u00a7 1.136(a). Substantively, it cures every defect raised in the Notice to File Missing Parts: it rectifies the inventor declaration defect under 37 CFR \u00a7 1.63(a)(4) via PTO/AIA/01; it executes a proactive, preemptive formalities cure by submitting a clean substitute specification under 37 CFR \u00a7 1.125(c), a marked-up copy, and a verified no-new-matter certification under \u00a7 1.125(b), excising informal embedded drawings, claims, and abstract into compliant standalone documents under 37 CFR \u00a7\u00a7 1.75(h), 1.72(b), and 1.84. Furthermore, Candidate #2 executes the mathematically optimal Path B knapsack subset-sum fee allocation under 37 CFR \u00a7 1.22(b) and MPEP \u00a7 509\u2014directing $490.00 of the unapplied $520.00 deposit credit to basic filing ($70.00), examination ($352.00), and late surcharge ($68.00), leaving a clean $30.00 credit residual, while remitting fresh cash of $480.00 for the search fee and non-DOCX surcharge plus $60.00 for the conditional suspension petition fee. By presenting these actions with pristine technical precision, complete statutory recitations, and zero adversarial friction, Candidate #2 creates virtually zero risk of rejection or administrative bounce.",
    "unlikely_to_succeed_reasons": null,
